# Default Permissions (Modules & Roles)

## Permission vocabulary

Most modules expose:

- `view` — browse or access data
- `create` — add records
- `edit` / `update` — modify records
- `delete` — remove records
- `manage` — configuration and assignments within module scope
- `export` — export data or reports
- `assign` — assign records (patient to bed, staff to case)
- `approve` — workflow approvals
- Module-specific actions (e.g. `dispense`, `request`, `report`, `prescribe`)

## Permission attachment levels

Permissions attach at **user**, **role**, **module**, and **subscription package** levels. Users may hold multiple roles and module assignments.

**Effective permissions** = union(role grants ∪ module grants ∪ user grants) ∩ subscription package ∩ ABAC scope.

Never exceed the active subscription. Multiple roles expand the grant union, then subscription and ABAC still restrict.
This source-controlled vocabulary and its shipped assignments must seed a complete core permission set out of the box.

## ABAC scoping

Enforce Attribute-Based Access Control on every permission. Filter by user, record, department, facility, tenant, and context such as `own`, `assigned`, `department`, `facility`, `tenant`, `status`. Avoid generic `manage` / `view all` unless explicitly required and audited.

